{"term":"worthy","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:87ac3a95cdf302a85a","definition":"Having worth, merit, or value.","example":"These banished men that I have kept withal / Are men endued with worthy qualities","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["markworthy","noteworthy","worthily","worthiness","the laborer is worthy of his hire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4691705a94ed56cbe3","definition":"Admirable or honourable.","example":"that such iron moulds as these shall have autority to knaw out the choicest periods of exquisitest books, and to commit such a treacherous fraud against the orphan remainders of worthiest men after death, the more sorrow will belong to that haples race of men, whose misfortune it is to have understanding.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["esteemed","laudable","venerated","well-regarded","admired","applauded","blessed","distinguished","eminent","esteemed","feared","gloriful","glorious","honoured","illustrious","priceless","reputable","respected","revered","sacred","treasured","valued","venerated","well-regarded","worthy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["markworthy","noteworthy","worthily","worthiness","the laborer is worthy of his hire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2fe11c99d36f462748","definition":"Deserving, or having sufficient worth.","example":"1 And I saw in þe right hand of him that sate on the Throne, a booke written within, & on the backeside, sealed with seuen seales.\n2 And I saw a strong Angel proclaiming with a loude voice; Who is worthy to open the booke, and to loose the seales thereof?\n3 And no man in heauen, nor in earth, neither vnder the earth, was able to open the booke, neither to looke thereon.\n4 And I wept much, because no man was found worthy to open, and to reade the booke, neither to looke thereon.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["laudable","praiseworthy","venerable","admirable","allowable","commendable","creditable","estimable","glorious","honorable","laudable","praiseworthy","respectable","reverable","reverend","valuable","venerable","worthy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["markworthy","noteworthy","worthily","worthiness","the laborer is worthy of his hire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9a7f4399b55e1d5c40","definition":"Suited; suitable; befitting.","example":"No, Warwick, thou art worthy of the sway.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["markworthy","noteworthy","worthily","worthiness","the laborer is worthy of his hire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:48d35c5deddd886bb7","definition":"A distinguished or eminent person.","example":"That worthy one day, in our absence, being caught in the act of culpable talpicide, was rebuked by his mistress for disobeying his master's orders.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["markworthy","noteworthy","worthily","worthiness","the laborer is worthy of his hire","-worthy","unworthy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a0f4bb9248e0c6b9b","definition":"a good, wise and virtuous person.","example":"Confuciu